From 661a611a038b996498b8f7e76ba8a5a553703687 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Uzair Aftab <git@uzaaft.me>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:14:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] fix(xray): don't panic on an invalid filter regexp

Typing a filter into the Xray view that isn't a valid regular
expression, e.g. "/+foo" or "/?:cm", crashed k9s. rxFilter,
rxInverseFilter and the tree model's rxMatch all compiled the user's
query with regexp.MustCompile, so a parse error panicked inside the
draw loop.

They now use regexp.Compile and treat an invalid pattern as matching
nothing, the same way the describe, YAML and log filters already
handle it.

TestXrayRxFilterInvalidRegexp and TestRxMatchInvalidRegexp feed
invalid patterns to each function and fail without this change.
